    #      values check wants some value written by the anchor sample and some
    #      removed by the removal, which writes none (change LF's form).
    #  VJ. The run loop, the record pairs, the keep and the open check are SJ's
    #      and WJ's with this phase's names; reccheck.py takes the dropped
    #      families as an input beside the changed and added ones; the anchor
    #      record's families are derived from the --parts lines, the removal
    #      record's from its entries table, which the rule checked row by row
    #      (the rulings allow a row recompressed or changed); six record files
    #      installed, four when the keep is skipped.
    #  VK. UK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`; the sourced
    #      scripts/counting.sh, a committed script, runs one on the directory its
    #      counting controls make (allowed: a directory the script created in
    #      that run); the working directory and the keeps stand, kept, and
    #      Python writes no bytecode.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 6 P3 from M3 part 6 P2's run script (at the phase
    # commit d3c4a9c, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p2/run.log; its change lists
    # up to VK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary and the body from the survey to the corpus record pairs'
    # installation replaced whole (gen/run_block.sh, by its anchor lines, P2's
    # record check carried into it unchanged), and the body grepped afterwards
    # for P2's names, subjects, stems and the tokens imgcmp, imgsurvey,
    # m3p6-p2-, P1_REC and PREV_CB. What differs, and why:
    #  XA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/scripts, on the disk)
    #      and the keep (m3p6-p3/keep-host) are this phase's; the base is P2's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 6 P2 record:"); the phase commit is P3's tool
    #      commit by its subject ("M3 part 6 P3: emend-copy --copy-sample"); one
    #      sample, copy, with its run directory <runs>/<date>-<sha>-copy and its
    #      record stem m3p6-p3-<date>-<sha> (the spec's name), and three rerun
    #      directories <runs>/<date>-<sha>-anchor, -removeimage and -commentbox
    #      (RERUNS); SUPERSEDED_RUN names the four by their common stem; the
    #      spec pinned through SPEC_SHA at P3's doc commit, planning's rulings
    #      during P3 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy, printed.
    #  XB. Change VB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P2's, the last committed, named by its record
    #      commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6 P2 record:"; no hash is
    #      typed here); it is the base itself, the parent of P3's doc commit; the
    #      control names the doc commit instead. P2_REC names the same commit, the
    #      one whose run directories the reruns are compared with (change XF).
    #  XC. The comparison is copycmp.py, built for this phase (<home>/.cache/
    #      emend-build/m3p6-p3/gen/copycmp_build.py) with P2's imgcmp.py
    #      readers copied by name, one mode, copy, fifteen flags: whole_bytes,
    #      data_same, kept_same, views_same, setup_same, dropped_gone (the
    #      spec's copy check, and the copy built from S byte for byte),
    #      rels_set (ruling 1), comments_same and notes_placed (the spec's
    #      carried checks), workbook_sheet, types_set, chain_rule, rest_same,
    #      xml_values and flagged (P2's). The lines' relations are the spec's:
    #      one sheet more, the copy's counts its source's, no chain after a
    #      formula. The tool's counts equal the comparison's.
    #  XD. NEW, the survey (copysurvey.py, <scripts>, copied into <work> and
    #      printed) replaces VD's, in its form: <corpus> its parameter, every
    #      regular file of <corpus>/corpus listed, one wb line of twenty fields
    #      per workbook; the log checks its forms, prints the distributions and
    #      checks every line's figures against it, and the comparison's parts
    #      against it. No drawings line (no decision rests on one here).
    #  XE. Changes PE, QE, SE and VE (every row ok) stand. The entries rule is
    #      the rulings during P3's: the copy's entry added; its rels part added
    #      exactly when S has a hyperlink or a comments relationship (ruling 1);
    #      the comments and VML parts added when carried; the workbook part, its
    #      rels part and the content types changed, flagged descriptor at most;
    #      the chain's entry dropped exactly when S holds a formula and the
    #      workbook a chain; every other row identical and unflagged; nothing
    #      recompressed. Each allowance has a control that accepts it where it
    #      applies and one that refuses it where it does not. The summary's
    #      totals are checked against what the rows imply and against the
    #      entries table.
    #  XF. NEW, the three earlier samples once more on both targets, their
    #      outputs by sha256, their lines and their diff tables P2's runs' byte
    #      for byte (change VF's form for three samples), the run directories
    #      read from the "the run directories:" line of P2's run log at P2's
    #      record commit and checked against the run directory P2's committed
    #      anchor record names; no record pair is written for the reruns.
    #  XG. Change UG's no-row rule gives way: the copy makes the write a formula
    #      change when S holds a formula (specs/0013's rule, "The copy"), so
    #      each chain workbook's calcChain row is dropped exactly there, and is
    #      identical and unflagged elsewhere; some row is dropped.
    #  XH. Change PH (the open check's own TMPDIR device) stands, unchanged.
    #  XI. The plants: every flag's planted control runs on the first ok
    #      workbook in manifest order of the plain case (S's comments not
    #      carried) and of the carried case, each on its own check line, the
    #      plant turning its own flag; every flag has a plant on both cases.
    #      The xml values check wants some value written (the workbook's new
    #      sheet; change LF's form).
    #  XJ. The run loop, the record pair, the keep and the open check are VJ's
    #      with this phase's names; the record's families are derived from its
    #      entries table, which the rule checked row by row; four record files
    #      installed, two when the keep is skipped.
    #  XK. Ruling 8 of the planning rulings during P2 (build pruning) and
    #      ruling 10 of the planning rulings during P3 (one target root per
    #      phase, one subdirectory per source tree): the phase's target root is
    #      <target>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p3/target, and every build
    #      of <repo> by this script, dry or logged, goes into <target>/main
    #      (CARGO_TARGET_DIR), the subdirectory ruling 10 gives the main tree;
    #      this script builds from no other tree. P2's <build> placeholder (a
    #      run directory holding its own target) is gone with the input
    #      RUN_BUILD_ROOT, so no run moves the builds, and nothing here cleans
    #      them; the i686 keep is <work>/keep-i686, kept, not under the target.
    #      VK stands: this script runs no `rm -rf`.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 6 P4 from M3 part 6 P3's run script (at the phase
    # commit 6a90674, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p3/run.log; its change lists
    # up to XK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p4/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary replaced, the build section replaced by the size log's binaries,
    # the copy sample's record pair carried into the earlier samples' loop by
    # its anchor lines, and the body grepped afterwards for P3's names,
    # subjects and tokens. copycmp.py and copysurvey.py are P3's, copied beside
    # this script byte for byte. What differs, and why:
    #  YA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p4/scripts, on the disk)
    #      and the keep (m3p6-p4/keep-host) are this phase's; the base is P3's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 6 P3 record:"); the phase commit is P4's
    #      catalogue and probes commit by its subject ("M3 part 6 P4: the
    #      catalogue and limits, the probes"); the four samples each have a run
    #      directory <runs>/<date>-<sha>-<sample> and a record stem
    #      m3p6-p4-<sample>-<date>-<sha> (the spec's names, "P4"); SAMPLES is
    #      still the copy sample, whose checks are P3's, and RERUNS the three
    #      earlier samples; SUPERSEDED_RUN names the four by their common stem;
    #      the spec pinned through SPEC_SHA at P4's doc commit, planning's
    #      rulings during P4 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy,
    #      printed. The usage takes the size.log as its third argument.
    #  YB. Change XB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P3's, the last committed, named by its record
    #      commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6 P3 record:"; no hash is
    #      typed here); it is the base itself, the parent of P4's doc commit; the
    #      control names the doc commit instead. P3_REC names the same commit,
    #      the one whose run directories the four samples are compared with
    #      (change YF).
    #  YC. Part 5 P3's change RC: the release binaries are the size log's, run
    #      where it built them (<target>/main/release and
    #      <target>/main/i686-unknown-linux-musl/release, the main tree's subdirectory, ruling 10
    #      of the planning rulings during P3), each hashed here and compared with
    #      its "hash: <name> <target> <sha256>" line in the size.log given, none
    #      built here; the size.log checked to be this phase's at this phase
    #      commit and to end all as expected. The run row's binaries are checked
    #      against the same hashes as before.
    #  YD. The survey (change XD) and the comparison (change XC) are P3's, byte
    #      for byte, run over the copy sample as P3's run did.
    #  YE. The earlier samples' rows: every row ok, every input and output
    #      opening in LibreOffice with no leftover, and the summary's status
    #      totals the entries table's; their entry rules are P2's and P1's, and
    #      hold here because every diff table is P3's run's byte for byte
    #      (change YF), whose run log checked them against P2's runs, which
    #      checked the rules.
    #  YF. Change XF's form for four samples: every sample, the copy sample
    #      included, compared on both targets with P3's run directory for it,
    #      its outputs by sha256, its lines and its diff tables byte for byte,
    #      every workbook's outcome and exit equal; the run directories read
    #      from the "the run directories:" line of P3's run log at P3's record
    #      commit and checked against the run directory P3's committed copy
    #      record names.
    #  YJ. Change XJ's record pair for each of the four samples: the copy
    #      sample's as P3's, and the three earlier samples' through the same
    #      record script and record check, their families derived from their
    #      entries tables; ten record files installed, eight when the keep is
    #      skipped.
    #  YK. Ruling 8 of the planning rulings during P2 and ruling 10 of those
    #      during P3: the phase's target root is <target>, <home>/.cache/
    #      emend-build/m3p6-p4/target; the keep's tests build into <target>/main
    #      (CARGO_TARGET_DIR), where size.log built the release binaries this
    #      log runs; nothing here cleans it. VK stands: this script runs no
    #      `rm -rf`.
    #
    #
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 7 P3 from M3 part 6 P4's run script (at the phase
    # commit 9cfd92e, printed in records/logs/m3p6-p4/run.log; its change lists
    # up to YK are above), generated by <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/gen/
    # run.py, every replacement asserted to occur as often as it says, the top
    # summary replaced, the keep and open-check sections removed, and the body
    # grepped afterwards for part 6 P4's names, subjects and tokens.
    # copycmp.py and copysurvey.py are part 6 P4's, copied beside this script
    # byte for byte. What differs, and why:
    #  RNA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the script directory
    #       (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/scripts, on the disk)
    #       are this phase's; the base is part 7 P2's record commit ("M3 part 7
    #       P2 record:"); the phase commit is P3's code commit by its subject
    #       ("M3 part 7 P3: rust-version equal to the pin, and the gate checks
    #       the pins agree"); the four samples each have a run directory
    #       <runs>/<date>-<sha>-<sample> and a record stem
    #       m3p7-p3-<sample>-<date>-<sha> (specs/0029 "Harness runs"); the spec
    #       is specs/0029, pinned through SPEC_SHA at this phase's doc commit. The usage
    #       takes the size.log as its second argument, and no test.log.
    #  RNB. The run directories the four samples are compared with are part 6
    #       P4's, named by its record commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6
    #       P4 record:"; no hash is typed here), an ancestor of the phase commit,
    #       read from the "the run directories:" line of part 6 P4's run log at
    #       that commit and checked against the run directory its committed copy
    #       record names.
    #  RNC. The keep and the open check go, with their inputs (RUN_KEEP,
    #       RUN_SKIP_KEEP, SUPERSEDED_KEEP), the test.log argument, the <keep>
    #       root and the open record's stem: specs/0029 "Harness runs" names the
    #       four samples alone. The record files installed are the four pairs,
    #       eight.
    #  RND. Each sample's record header names its binaries (specs/0029 item 5):
    #       the .md holds one "- Binaries (host)" and one "- Binaries (i686)"
    #       line whose two hashes are the binaries this log ran, with a control.
    #  RNE. The size.log is this phase's (its "about:" line names P3's phase
    #       commit).
    #  RNF. The phase's target root is <target>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/
    #       m3p7-p3/target (specs/0001 "Rules for every phase", one target root
    #       per phase); this log builds nothing and runs the release binaries
    #       size.log built in <target>/main.
    #  RNG. The runner gives each child its own TMPDIR under its own work
    #       directory, under <work>/tmp-run here (specs/0029 P1 ruling 2); the
    #       check that <work>/tmp-run is empty after each run stands.
    #
    # Usage: m8p2-p4-run.sh <phase commit> <gate log> > <file outside the tree>;
    # the caller moves the output to records/logs/m8p2-p4/run.log (change WS).
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/run.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    GATE_LOG=${2:?the gate log required}
    # Every environment input, as it was set, before any is unset (changes RU, TC,
    # TQ, TT, WE and WV: P3's size log path, WP's, is gone; the records'
    # destination, RUN_RECORDS_DEST, is a dry run's override).
    INPUT_NAMES="RERUN_NOTE RERUN_FILES PLANNING_SPEC RUN_RELEASE_DIR RUN_CORPUS RUN_OUT_ROOT RUN_FLAGS RUN_TMPDIR RUN_RECORDS_DEST EMEND_COPY_KEEP_OUTPUT EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR HOME"
    OVERRIDES="RUN_RELEASE_DIR RUN_CORPUS RUN_OUT_ROOT RUN_FLAGS RUN_TMPDIR RUN_RECORDS_DEST"
    declare -A INPUT_SEEN
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do
      if [ -n "${!v+x}" ]; then INPUT_SEEN[$v]=${!v}; else INPUT_SEEN[$v]=unset; fi
    done
    LOGGED=yes
    for v in $OVERRIDES; do
      if [ "${INPUT_SEEN[$v]}" != unset ]; then LOGGED=no; fi
    done
    CORPUS=${RUN_CORPUS:-$HOME/emend-testing}
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never
    # Python writes no bytecode, so nothing arises to be removed.
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    # Every cargo command of this log runs offline; the two settings are printed below.
    export CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true
    # Change TT: the keep-output variable of P1 is never given to these runs.
    unset EMEND_KEEP_DIR EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_COPY_KEEP_OUTPUT RUSTDOCFLAGS RUSTFLAGS
    IMAGE=localhost/emend-lo:25.2.3-2-deb13u6
    # The open check's timeout and the runner's timeout, part 1 P2's (specs/0047
    # "The reruns (P2)"), kept.
    LO_TIMEOUT_S=600
    TIMEOUT_S=300
    SPEC=specs/0048-the-two-refusals.md
    # Change WS: the committed blob the doc commit holds (planning's P4 brief;
    # the generator asserts it).
    SPEC_WANT=e3aaf65402a1b8b22f06e4f28c5011ee033e5b0a0b9ac74babddc6109c8f85f8
    PLANNING_SPEC=${PLANNING_SPEC:-}
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m8p2-p4
    # The phase's one target root; the gate built the release binaries into
    # <target>/main (no build here).
    TARGET_ROOT=$PHASE_DIR/target
    BUILD_ROOT=$TARGET_ROOT/main
    RELEASE_DIR=${RUN_RELEASE_DIR:-$BUILD_ROOT/release}
    # Change WV: the record pairs are installed into records/ (part 1 P2's
    # section 5, printed in records/logs/m8p1-p2/run.log; P3's change WE
    # reversed); a dry run names its own directory with RUN_RECORDS_DEST.
    RECORDS_DEST=${RUN_RECORDS_DEST:-records}
    # Change WC: the earlier record of every run is part 1 P2's at 8816db0
    # (specs/0048 "Harness runs").
    PREV_TAG=2026-11-09-8816db0
    # Change WU: the expected-change table, as specs/0048 "Harness runs" names it
    # for P1, P2 and P3 and P4 reruns: <name>:<id>:<then>:<now>, each triple
    # outcome/lo/lo_in, a then and a now per pair; the pair named unchanged,
    # <name>:<id>:<then> (decision 2 A); the remove pair's line reads the removed
    # count 0 and removed_reason pivot_source (decision 3 A).
    EXPECTED_TABLE="delete-rows:90a5b01f9541:error/-/ok:ok/ok/ok delete-columns:91d2bdffa46a:error/-/ok:ok/ok/ok comment:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok:ok/ok/ok richcomment:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok:ok/ok/ok commentbox:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok:ok/ok/ok remove:495c7b79b183:ok/fail/ok:ok/ok/ok"
    KEPT_TABLE="copy:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok"
    EXPECT_REMOVED=0
    EXPECT_REASON=pivot_source
    # pair_key <entry>: its <name>:<id>; entry_then and entry_now <entry>: its
    # then-triple and its now-triple (empty for a pair named unchanged).
    pair_key() { local n=${1%%:*} r=${1#*:}; printf '%s:%s\n' "$n" "${r%%:*}"; }
    entry_then() { local r=${1#*:}; r=${r#*:}; printf '%s\n' "${r%%:*}"; }
    entry_now() { local r=${1#*:}; r=${r#*:}; case $r in *:*) printf '%s\n' "${r#*:}" ;; *) printf '\n' ;; esac; }
    EXPECTED_PAIRS=$(for e in $EXPECTED_TABLE; do pair_key "$e"; done | tr '\n' ' ')
    KEPT_PAIRS=$(for e in $KEPT_TABLE; do pair_key "$e"; done | tr '\n' ' ')
    # table_entry <name>:<id>: the table's entry for the pair, empty when none.
    table_entry() { local e; for e in $EXPECTED_TABLE $KEPT_TABLE; do if [ "$(pair_key "$e")" = "$1" ]; then printf '%s\n' "$e"; return 0; fi; done; return 0; }
    RUN_OUT_ROOT=${RUN_OUT_ROOT:-$CORPUS/runs}
    # Change WT: the passthrough and every sample the usage text names but
    # --new-sample (part 1 P2's section 2); a dry run may name a subset with
    # RUN_FLAGS.
    RUN_FLAGS=${RUN_FLAGS:-}
    if [ ! -f "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" ] || [ ! -d "$CORPUS/corpus" ]; then echo "the corpus directory holds no manifest.tsv and corpus/" >&2; exit 2; fi
    SHORT=$(git rev-parse --short=7 "$C")
    DATE=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%d)
    RUN=$DATE-$SHORT
    # TMPDIR is <scratch>/tmp, the phase's directory's, made and exported before
    # any mktemp; the working directory is the one mktemp -d makes under it, on
    # the disk, kept; nothing here is removed.
    TMPDIR=$PHASE_DIR/tmp
    # Change TQ, carried (specs/0047 ruling A): a dry run names its own with
    # RUN_TMPDIR.
    if [ -n "${RUN_TMPDIR:-}" ]; then TMPDIR=$RUN_TMPDIR; fi
    export TMPDIR
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" || exit 2
    B=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2
    mkdir "$B/bin" "$B/records" "$B/tmp-run" "$B/prev" || exit 2
    RECORDS=$B/records
    RUNTMP=$B/tmp-run
    # The counting library is the phase commit's, by git show.
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    sha_of() { sha256sum <"$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    if [ ! -f "$GATE_LOG" ]; then echo "the gate log is not a file" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    # Change WS: what the status pattern admits: this phase's log directory, its
    # record files at this commit (change WV), and planning's modified specs/0048
    # and ROADMAP.md; nothing else.
    OURS="^((\\?\\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m8p2-p4/|\\?\\? records/m8p2-[a-z0-9-]+-$DATE-$SHORT[.](md|txt)\$| M specs/0048-the-two-refusals[.]md\$| M ROADMAP[.]md\$)"
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs and planning's spec" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    
    # Change RV: the gate's release binaries, copied into <work>/bin; the copies
    # are what this log runs.
    for b in emend-copy xlsx-diff; do
      if [ ! -x "$RELEASE_DIR/$b" ]; then echo "the gate's release $b is not there" >&2; exit 2; fi
      cp "$RELEASE_DIR/$b" "$B/bin/$b" || exit 2
    done
    PT=$B/bin/emend-copy
    XD=$B/bin/xlsx-diff
    # Change RW: the flags, from the binary's own usage text (part 1's ruling E): its
    # usage error, the run with no argument, read for every word ending in
    # -sample, in its order.
    "$PT" >"$B/usage.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    USAGE_RC=$?
    LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E -- '--[a-z0-9-]*-sample' "$B/usage.out" >"$B/usage.flags"
    : >"$B/run.flags"
    # Change WT: every flag of the usage text but --new-sample (part 1 P2's
    # form), in its order; a dry run's RUN_FLAGS names a subset.
    while IFS= read -r f; do
      [ "$f" = --new-sample ] && continue
      if [ -n "$RUN_FLAGS" ]; then
        case " $RUN_FLAGS " in *" $f "*) ;; *) continue ;; esac
      fi
      printf '%s\n' "$f" >>"$B/run.flags"
    done <"$B/usage.flags"
    if [ -n "$RUN_FLAGS" ]; then
      for f in $RUN_FLAGS; do
        if [ "$(count_matches -xF "$f" "$B/run.flags")" != 1 ]; then echo "RUN_FLAGS names $f, which is not a sample the usage text names (or is --new-sample)" >&2; exit 2; fi
      done
    fi
    name_of() { local n=${1#--}; printf '%s\n' "${n%-sample}"; }
    # The run directories and record files this log writes, each refused if it
    # is there already: the passthrough's first, then each flag's (change TD;
    # changes WT and WV).
    { echo passthrough; while IFS= read -r f; do name_of "$f"; done <"$B/run.flags"; } >"$B/run.names"
    while IFS= read -r n; do
      if [ -e "$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$n" ]; then echo "$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$n is already there; name a fresh run" >&2; exit 2; fi
      for x in md txt; do
        if [ -e "$RECORDS_DEST/m8p2-$n-$RUN.$x" ]; then echo "$RECORDS_DEST/m8p2-$n-$RUN.$x is already there; move it aside first" >&2; exit 2; fi
      done
    done <"$B/run.names"
    
    # The runs root before the corpus, the phase's directories before <phase>,
    # and <home> last. Change WP: no probe is built here, so no probe root.
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$B#<work>#g" -e "s#$TMPDIR#<scratch>/tmp#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_ROOT#<target>#g" -e "s#$RUN_OUT_ROOT#<runs>#g" -e "s#$CORPUS#<corpus>#g" \
        -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "about: M8 part 2 P4 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    # The environment inputs, each on its labelled line.
    for v in $INPUT_NAMES; do echo "input: $v=${INPUT_SEEN[$v]}"; done
    echo "input (as exported by this script): PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=$PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=$CARGO_NET_OFFLINE"
    echo "input: TMPDIR=$TMPDIR"
    echo "  (TMPDIR set, made and exported by this script before any mktemp; <work> is made under it)"
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo "input: the gate log (the second argument): $GATE_LOG"
    if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then
      echo "mode: the logged run: none of the dry run's overrides is set ($OVERRIDES), so the whole set's counts and the expected-change totals are judged (changes TC and WG)"
    else
      echo "mode: a dry run, a DRY CUT (changes TC and WG; specs/0043 ruling Q): an override is set; the counts of the whole set and the expected-change totals are not judged, an earlier id missing from the fictional corpus is printed and not judged, and nothing is written under the real corpus's runs/ unless an override left it there"
    fi
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    # Change NTJ: the fourth shape, PYB: a Python call without -I -B (the word
    # followed by whitespace and an option or a .py path, outside a comment,
    # and not by " -I -B"). The word is built from two halves, so that this
    # form's own text is no call.
    PYW=pyth
    PYW=${PYW}on3
    pyb_count() {
      awk -v w="$PYW" '{ l = $0; sub(/^[ \t]+/, "", l); if (substr(l, 1, 1) == "#") next; s = l
        while ((i = index(s, w)) > 0) { r = substr(s, i + length(w)); if (r ~ /^[ \t]+(-|[^ \t]*[.]py([ \t"]|$))/ && r !~ /^ -I -B( |$)/) { n++; break }; s = r }
      } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    printf '%s\n' "$PYW -c x" "$PYW -I -B -c x" "# $PYW -c x" "command -v $PYW" "$PYW tool.py" >"$B/pyb-fixture"
    n_self=$(pyb_count "$SELF")
    n_fix=$(pyb_count "$B/pyb-fixture")
    echo "command: pyb_count <this script>, and the same over a fixture of five lines: a call with -c, one with -I -B -c, a comment, a command -v, a call of a .py path"
    echo "  shape PYB: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
    check "PYB: this script holds none (change NTJ)" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
    check "control: PYB: the same form finds the fixture's two calls without -I -B and not its other three lines" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 2 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    BASE=$(by_subject 'M8 part 2 P3 record: the size record, the logs, the README, the check')
    DOC=$(by_subject 'M8 part 2 P4: commit planning docs (the P3 verification and rulings)')
    CODE=$(by_subject "M8 part 2 P4: the README's figures, the CHANGELOG clause and the crate docs' sentence")
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's subject>, for each role"
    echo "  P3's record commit (the base): ${BASE:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC:-none}"
    echo "  the documents commit, the phase commit (the README's figures, the CHANGELOG clause, the crate docs' sentence; rulings H, K (4) and M (1)): ${CODE:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~2"
    for k in 0 1 2; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    # Change WS: the documents commit, the doc commit and the base, each the
    # next's child.
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$CODE" "$DOC" "$BASE"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the documents commit, the doc commit and the base, each the next's child, the documents commit the phase commit (change WS)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local CODE=$DOC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the phase commit (change WS)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    roles_ctl2() { local DOC=$BASE BASE=$DOC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit and the base swapped (change WS)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl2)"
    roles_ctl3() { local BASE=; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses a role that resolved to nothing" "$(ynnot roles_ctl3)"
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "  the controls' commits: the null commit $NULL_SHA; the fabricated commit $FAKE_SHA (the given one, its last hex digit changed); the short sha $SHORT"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "the phase commit is the documents commit, by its subject (change WS)" "$(yn [ "$CODE" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the doc commit" "$(ynnot [ "$DOC" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the base" "$(ynnot [ "$BASE" = "$C" ])"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a fabricated commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$FAKE_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$SHORT")"
    short_names_head() { [ "$(git rev-parse "$SHORT")" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ]; }
    check "control: the short sha is the real commit's, so only its form is refused" "$(yn short_names_head)"
    echo "phase: Milestone 8 part 2 P4 ($SPEC) run.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above, with the directory it is kept in"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s  kept in %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time (named in %s)\n' "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
    fi
    # Change WG: ruling F's RERUN_NOTE requirement (TZ) is not this phase's;
    # every file RERUN_FILES names is there.
    rerun_files_there() {
      local sf
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do [ -f "$sf" ] || return 1; done
    }
    echo "  logged run: $LOGGED; RERUN_NOTE set: $([ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no); files RERUN_FILES names: $(set -- ${RERUN_FILES:-}; echo $#)"
    check "every file RERUN_FILES names is there (changes TZ and WG)" "$(yn rerun_files_there)"
    rerun_files_ctl() { local RERUN_FILES="$MAIN/no-such-file-wg"; rerun_files_there; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a file that is not there" "$(ynnot rerun_files_ctl)"
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this run builds nothing (the gate built the release binaries)"
    no_build_running() { [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ]; }
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn no_build_running)"
    echo "DETACHED: no interactive call waits on this run; stdout and stderr go to a file, polled from later calls."
    echo "SETTINGS CHOSEN BEFORE THE RUN, never tuned during it: every run --label host --timeout $TIMEOUT_S --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S, the runner's default memory; the i686 label, the scale tiers and the openpyxl comparison are not run, and no Excel run (specs/0048 \"Harness runs\" P4)"
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, scrubbed after the corpus's paths); scripts/counting.sh, tools/emend-copy/src/main.rs, the spec and the records read are taken from it at the phase commit by git show; scripts/passthrough-run.sh and scripts/passthrough-record.py are run from it, each checked equal to the phase commit's (the runner sources scripts/lo-check.sh, checked too); the record pairs are installed into its records/ unless RUN_RECORDS_DEST names a dry run's directory (change WV)"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m8p2-p4 on the disk, the phase's directory; <phase>/gen holds the generator that wrote this script and <phase>/model the template it was written from"
    echo "root: <scratch> stands for <phase>, the phase's directory, named <scratch> where TMPDIR is concerned: TMPDIR is <scratch>/tmp (a dry run's RUN_TMPDIR otherwise, change TQ), made and exported by this script before any mktemp, and <work> is made under it"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <phase>/scripts on the disk, this script's own directory; this script's own standard error goes to <scripts>/out/run.stderr (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <work> stands for this run's working directory, made by mktemp -d under TMPDIR, <scratch>/tmp, on the disk (the counting library, the binaries' copies <work>/bin, the record pairs before they are installed, <work>/records, the runs' TMPDIR <work>/tmp-run, the earlier records read at the phase commit <work>/prev, the checks' programs and outputs), kept after the run and never removed"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <phase>/target on the disk, the phase's one target root: the gate built the release binaries into <target>/main/release"
    echo "root: <corpus> stands for the private corpus directory unless RUN_CORPUS names a fictional one for a dry run (its manifest.tsv and the inputs under <corpus>/corpus, read by the runner)"
    echo "root: <runs> stands for the corpus run directories' parent, <corpus>/runs unless RUN_OUT_ROOT names another for a dry run; this log's run directories <runs>/$RUN-<name> are written there"
    echo "root: <id> stands for a directory of an earlier phase's log and appears in this log only in the printed script's carried history; this log reads and writes nothing under it (change WM)"
    echo "root: <source> stands for a directory of an earlier phase's log and appears in this log only in the printed script's carried history; this log reads and writes nothing under it (change WM)"
    echo "root: <stage> stands for a directory of an earlier phase's log and appears in this log only in the printed script's carried history; this log reads and writes nothing under it (change WM)"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() {
      local a b all=("$SELF_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" "$CORPUS" "$TMPDIR")
      for a in "${all[@]}"; do for b in "${all[@]}"; do
        [ "$a" = "$b" ] && continue
        apart "$a" "$b" || return 1
      done; done
    }
    check "the roots other than <home>, <phase>, <work> and <runs> are distinct, none inside another (TMPDIR, <scratch>/tmp, among them)" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    work_in_tmpdir() { case "$B/" in "$TMPDIR/"*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    check "<work>, the directory mktemp -d made, is under TMPDIR, <scratch>/tmp" "$(yn work_in_tmpdir)"
    work_ctl() { local B=/tmp/x; work_in_tmpdir; }
    check "control: the same test refuses a working directory under /tmp" "$(ynnot work_ctl)"
    # Every mktemp call of this script is checked under TMPDIR, so the source is
    # read for its calls outside comments; the call's text is built from
    # pieces, so this form's own text is no call.
    MKW='$('
    MKW=${MKW}mkt
    MKW=${MKW}emp
    count_tempcalls() {
      awk -v w="$MKW" '{ l = $0; sub(/^[ \t]+/, "", l); if (substr(l, 1, 1) == "#") next; s = l
        while ((i = index(s, w)) > 0) { n++; s = substr(s, i + length(w)) }
      } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"
    }
    printf '%s\n' "A=$MKW -d)" "F=$MKW)" "# $MKW -d)" >"$B/mktemp-fixture"
    n_mk=$(count_tempcalls "$SELF")
    n_mk_fix=$(count_tempcalls "$B/mktemp-fixture")
    echo "command: count_tempcalls <this script>, and the same over a fixture of three lines: a directory call, a file call, a comment"
    echo "  mktemp calls in this script outside comments: $n_mk (the one that makes <work>, checked under TMPDIR above); in the fixture: $n_mk_fix"
    check "this script makes one mktemp call, <work>'s, and no plain temporary file" "$(yn [ "$n_mk" = 1 ])"
    check "control: the same count finds the fixture's two calls and not its comment" "$(yn [ "$n_mk_fix" = 2 ])"
    runs_apart() { apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$RUN_OUT_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR"; }
    check "<runs> lies outside <repo> and <scripts>" "$(yn runs_apart)"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(ynnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them admitted by the phase's pattern (this phase's logs, its record files, planning's modified specs/0048 and ROADMAP.md) $entry_ours; the lines:"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    ours_ctl() { printf ' M scripts/check.sh\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified gate file" "$(ynnot ours_ctl)"
    ours_rec_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m8p2-p4/run.log\n M specs/0048-the-two-refusals.md\n?? records/m8p2-remove-%s-%s.md\n?? records/m8p2-passthrough-%s-%s.txt\n M ROADMAP.md\n?? records/m8p2-remove-%s-abcdef0.md\n M records/m8p2-edit-%s-%s.md\n?? records/m8p1-remove-%s-%s.txt\n?? records/logs/m8p2-p3/run.log\n?? records/size-m8p2-%s-%s.md\n M specs/0047-harness-findings.md\n M scripts/passthrough-record.py\n' "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" "$DATE" "$SHORT" | count_matches -E "$OURS" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern admits this phase's log, its record files at this commit and planning's specs/0048 and ROADMAP.md alone; it refuses a record of another commit, a modified record, another phase's record, another phase's log, a size record, another spec and a source file (changes WS and WV)" "$(yn [ "$(ours_rec_ctl)" = 5 ])"
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources (the phase commit's, by git show)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    echo
    echo "## the scripts, against the phase commit, and planning's uncommitted spec"
    tree_is_commit() { [ "$(sha_of "$1")" = "$(git show "$C:$1" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" ]; }
    for s in scripts/passthrough-run.sh scripts/passthrough-record.py scripts/lo-check.sh; do
      check "$s in the main tree is the phase commit's (sha256 $(sha_of "$s"))" "$(yn tree_is_commit "$s")"
    done
    tree_ctl() { [ "$(git show "$C:scripts/lo-check.sh" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$(sha_of scripts/passthrough-run.sh)" ]; }
    check "control: the same hash comparison tells two different scripts apart" "$(ynnot tree_ctl)"
    spec_now=$(sha_of "$SPEC")
    spec_committed=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum; sha256sum $SPEC (the working file: with PLANNING_SPEC set, planning's copy at that hash; unset, the phase commit's; change WM)"
    echo "  at the phase commit: $spec_committed; the pin: $SPEC_WANT"
    echo "  the working tree's copy: sha256 $spec_now"
    spec_ok() { [ "$spec_committed" = "$SPEC_WANT" ]; }
    check "the spec at the phase commit is at the pinned hash, the doc commit's blob" "$(yn spec_ok)"
    spec_ctl() { local spec_committed=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; spec_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the spec against another hash" "$(ynnot spec_ctl)"
    echo "input: PLANNING_SPEC: ${PLANNING_SPEC:-unset} (the working spec's sha256 when planning gives one; change WA)"
    # Change WA: set, the working spec hashes to it; unset, the working spec is
    # the phase commit's.
    working_ok() {
      if [ -n "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; then [ "$spec_now" = "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; else [ "$spec_now" = "$spec_committed" ]; fi
    }
    check "the working spec is the file PLANNING_SPEC names, or the phase commit's when it is unset (change WA)" "$(yn working_ok)"
    working_ctl() { local PLANNING_SPEC=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; working_ok; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses another hash named as PLANNING_SPEC" "$(ynnot working_ctl)"
    working_unset_ctl() { local PLANNING_SPEC= spec_now=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; working_ok; }
    check "control: with PLANNING_SPEC unset, the same comparison refuses a working copy that is not the phase commit's" "$(ynnot working_unset_ctl)"
    echo "command: podman image exists $IMAGE"
    check "the pinned LibreOffice image is there" "$(yn podman image exists "$IMAGE")"
    
    echo
    echo "## TMPDIR for the corpus runs, on the disk (part 6 P4's change LG)"
    dev_tmp=$(stat -c %d "$RUNTMP")
    dev_corpus=$(stat -c %d "$CORPUS/corpus")
    dev_proc=$(stat -c %d /proc)
    echo "command: stat -c %d <work>/tmp-run <corpus>/corpus /proc"
    echo "  device of TMPDIR (<work>/tmp-run): $dev_tmp; of the corpus directory (<corpus>/corpus): $dev_corpus; of /proc (the control): $dev_proc"
    check "TMPDIR for the corpus runs and the corpus directory are on one device" "$(yn [ "$dev_tmp" = "$dev_corpus" ])"
    dev_ctl() { if [ "$dev_proc" = "$dev_corpus" ]; then return 1; else return 0; fi; }
    check "control: the same comparison tells /proc's device from the corpus directory's" "$(yn dev_ctl)"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## 1. the binaries: the gate's release builds, copied into <work>/bin (change RV)"
    echo "command: cp <target>/main/release/<name> <work>/bin/<name>, for emend-copy and xlsx-diff (done before the log began); sha256sum each; the gate log's line for each, read by sed"
    bins_ok=yes
    for b in emend-copy xlsx-diff; do
      have=$(sha_of "$B/bin/$b")
      orig=$(sha_of "$RELEASE_DIR/$b")
      logged=$(sed -n "s#^  <target>/main/release/$b: sha256 \\([0-9a-f]\\{64\\}\\), bytes [0-9]*\$#\\1#p" "$GATE_LOG")
      n_logged=$(printf '%s\n' "$logged" | awk 'NF' | wc -l)
      echo "  <work>/bin/$b: sha256 $have, bytes $(stat -c %s "$B/bin/$b"); <target>/main/release/$b: sha256 $orig; the gate log's line: ${logged:-none} (lines $n_logged)"
      bin_ok() { [ "$n_logged" = 1 ] && [ "$have" = "$logged" ] && [ "$have" = "$orig" ]; }
      if bin_ok; then :; else bins_ok=no; fi
      check "$b: the copy is the gate's release binary, by the one line the gate log prints for it (change RV)" "$(yn bin_ok)"
    done
    bin_ctl() { local have=1111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111111; bin_ok; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses another hash" "$(ynnot bin_ctl)"
    if [ -x "$MAIN/target/release/emend-copy" ]; then
      stale_n=$("$MAIN/target/release/emend-copy" 2>&1 </dev/null | LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E -- '--[a-z0-9-]*-sample' | count_lines /dev/stdin)
      echo "  <repo>/target/release/emend-copy: there, built $(date -u -r "$MAIN/target/release/emend-copy" +%Y-%m-%d), its usage text names $stale_n flags ending in -sample; NOT USED by this log"
    else
      echo "  <repo>/target/release/emend-copy: not there; NOT USED by this log"
    fi
    if [ "$bins_ok" != yes ]; then
      echo "STOPPED: a binary is not the gate's; no run is made"
      exec 1>&3
      wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
      exit 1
    fi
    
    echo
    echo "## 2. the flag list, from the binary's own usage text (change RW, kept)"
    echo "command: <work>/bin/emend-copy (no argument): exit $USAGE_RC; grep -o -E -- '--[a-z0-9-]*-sample' over its output, in order"
    n_usage=$(count_lines "$B/usage.flags")
    n_usage_u=$(LC_ALL=C sort -u "$B/usage.flags" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    awk '{ print "    " NR ". " $0 }' "$B/usage.flags"
    echo "  the usage text's flags ending in -sample: $n_usage; distinct: $n_usage_u"
    check "the binary's usage error exits 2 (EXIT_ERROR)" "$(yn [ "$USAGE_RC" = 2 ])"
    check "every flag the usage text names is named once" "$(yn [ "$n_usage" = "$n_usage_u" ])"
    git show "$C:tools/emend-copy/src/main.rs" | awk '/^const USAGE: &str = /, /";$/' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E -- '--[a-z0-9-]*-sample' >"$B/usage-src.flags"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:tools/emend-copy/src/main.rs, the USAGE constant's lines (awk from 'const USAGE' to the line ending '\";'), the same grep: $(count_lines "$B/usage-src.flags") flags"
    check "the binary's flags, in order, are the USAGE constant's at the phase commit" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/usage.flags" "$B/usage-src.flags")"
    head -n -1 "$B/usage-src.flags" >"$B/c-usage.flags"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the list less its last flag" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$B/usage.flags" "$B/c-usage.flags")"
    # Change WT: --new-sample is named once and not run; --drop-calc-chain is in
    # the usage text and not among the flags run (part 1 P2's checks).
    check "--new-sample is in the usage text, and is excluded (specs/0016, P2: it writes its own input)" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF --new-sample "$B/usage.flags")" = 1 ])"
    check "--new-sample is not among the flags run" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF --new-sample "$B/run.flags")" = 0 ])"
    dcc_in_usage=$(count_matches -F '--drop-calc-chain' "$B/usage.out")
    echo "  --drop-calc-chain in the usage text: $dcc_in_usage line(s); it ends in no -sample, so the grep takes it nowhere (specs/0029 P5 verification ruling 1)"
    dcc_out() { [ "$dcc_in_usage" = 1 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F '--drop-calc-chain' "$B/run.flags")" = 0 ]; }
    check "--drop-calc-chain is in the usage text and is not among the flags run" "$(yn dcc_out)"
    n_run=$(count_lines "$B/run.flags")
    echo "  the flags run, in the usage text's order: $n_run"
    awk '{ print "    " NR ". " $0 }' "$B/run.flags"
    if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then
      check "every flag of the usage text but --new-sample is run ($n_run of $n_usage; change WT)" "$(yn [ "$n_run" = "$((n_usage - 1))" ])"
      check "the usage text names 59 such flags, so 58 are run, the 58 samples of specs/0048 \"Harness runs\" P4 (change WT)" "$(yn [ "$n_usage $n_run" = "59 58" ])"
    else
      echo "  RUN_FLAGS (a dry run): $n_run of the usage text's $n_usage run; the whole set's count is not judged"
    fi
    order_kept() { [ "$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -n -x -F -f "$B/run.flags" "$B/usage.flags" | cut -d: -f2 | tr '\n' ' ')" = "$(tr '\n' ' ' <"$B/run.flags")" ]; }
    check "the flags run keep the usage text's order" "$(yn order_kept)"
    
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # The helpers of the runs and the comparison. Outcome counts of a summary,
    # by the outcome column found by its header name: "error 1 ok 26 " and so
    # on, one pair per outcome, sorted.
    outcome_counts() { awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "outcome") o = i; next } o { n[$o]++ } END { for (k in n) print k, n[k] }' "$1" | LC_ALL=C sort | tr '\n' ' '; }
    # run_field <run.host.tsv> <column>: the one run row's value of the column,
    # found by its header name.
    run_field() { awk -F'\t' -v c="$2" 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == c) k = i; next } k { print $k }' "$1"; }
    # Change TF: triples <table>: the host rows of a record's .txt first table
    # (its lines up to the first blank line) or of a summary.host.tsv, as
    # "id<TAB>outcome<TAB>lo<TAB>lo_in", sorted by id; an empty lo or lo_in
    # cell reads "-".
    triples() { awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) k[$i] = i; next } $0 == "" { exit } $k["label"] == "host" { l = $k["lo"]; li = $k["lo_in"]; print $k["id"], $k["outcome"], (l == "" ? "-" : l), (li == "" ? "-" : li) }' "$1" | LC_ALL=C sort; }
    # compare_ids <earlier triples> <now triples> <out>: one line per id of
    # either, "same|changed|missing|new<TAB>id<TAB>then<TAB>now", each triple
    # written outcome/lo/lo_in, "-" for the side that lacks the id.
    compare_ids() { awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' 'FNR == NR { t[$1] = $2 "/" $3 "/" $4; next } { n[$1] = $2 "/" $3 "/" $4 } END { for (i in t) { if (!(i in n)) print "missing", i, t[i], "-"; else if (t[i] == n[i]) print "same", i, t[i], n[i]; else print "changed", i, t[i], n[i] } for (i in n) if (!(i in t)) print "new", i, "-", n[i] }' "$1" "$2" | LC_ALL=C sort -k2,2 >"$3"; }
    kind_count() { awk -F'\t' -v k="$2" '$1 == k { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # new_bad <comparison>: the new ids whose triple is not ok/ok/ok.
    new_bad() { awk -F'\t' '$1 == "new" && $4 != "ok/ok/ok" { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    printf 'id\tlabel\toutcome\tidentical\tlo\tlo_in\nw1\thost\tok\t3\tok\tok\nw2\thost\terror\t0\t\tok\nw3\thost\tok\t4\tfail\tok\nw1\ti686\tok\t3\tok\tok\n\nid\tother\nw9\thost\n' >"$B/c-then.tsv"
    printf 'id\tlabel\toutcome\tidentical\tlo\tlo_in\nw1\thost\tok\t3\tok\tok\nw3\thost\tok\t4\tok\tok\nw4\thost\tok\t1\tok\tok\nw5\thost\terror\t0\t\t\n\n' >"$B/c-now.tsv"
    triples "$B/c-then.tsv" >"$B/c-then.tri"
    triples "$B/c-now.tsv" >"$B/c-now.tri"
    compare_ids "$B/c-then.tri" "$B/c-now.tri" "$B/c-cmp"
    check "control: outcome_counts reads a fixture by its header (error 1, ok 3, both labels)" "$(yn [ "$(head -n 5 "$B/c-then.tsv" | outcome_counts /dev/stdin)" = "error 1 ok 3 " ])"
    check "control: triples reads the host rows up to the first blank line, an empty cell as - (3 rows; w2 error/-/ok)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/c-then.tri") $(awk -F'\t' '$1 == "w2" { print $2 "/" $3 "/" $4 }' "$B/c-then.tri")" = "3 error/-/ok" ])"
    cmp_ctl() { [ "$(kind_count "$B/c-cmp" same) $(kind_count "$B/c-cmp" changed) $(kind_count "$B/c-cmp" missing) $(kind_count "$B/c-cmp" new) $(new_bad "$B/c-cmp")" = "1 1 1 2 1" ]; }
    check "control: compare_ids over the two fixtures finds w1 the same, w3 changed, w2 missing, w4 and w5 new, and w5 the one new id not ok/ok/ok (TF)" "$(yn cmp_ctl)"
    # Change TE: the records at the phase commit whose first line is a step0
    # passthrough run's title, indexed by path, tool arguments ("none" when the
    # line is absent or says none) and record time.
    git grep -E '^(# step0 passthrough run |- Tool arguments: |- Record written: )' "$C" -- 'records/*.md' | sed "s#^$C:##" \
      | awk 'match($0, /[.]md:/) { p = substr($0, 1, RSTART + 2); r = substr($0, RSTART + 4); if (r ~ /^# step0 passthrough run /) s[p] = 1; else if (r ~ /^- Tool arguments: /) t[p] = substr(r, 19); else if (r ~ /^- Record written: /) w[p] = substr(r, 19) } END { for (p in s) if (p in w) print p "\t" ((p in t) ? t[p] : "none") "\t" w[p] }' \
      | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/rec-index.tsv"
    # pick_record <arguments>: the indexed record whose tool arguments are
    # exactly these, its name carrying no -scale-<tier>-, with the greatest
    # record time.
    pick_record() { awk -F'\t' -v f="$1" '$2 == f && $1 !~ /-scale-[a-z]-/ { if ($3 > best) { best = $3; p = $1 } } END { print p }' "$B/rec-index.tsv"; }
    printf 'records/a-x-2026-01-01-aaaaaaa.md\t--x-sample\t2026-01-01T00:00:00Z\nrecords/a-scale-b-x-2026-01-03-bbbbbbb.md\t--x-sample\t2026-01-03T00:00:00Z\nrecords/a-x-2026-01-02-ccccccc.md\t--x-sample --other\t2026-01-05T00:00:00Z\nrecords/z-x-2026-01-02-ddddddd.md\t--x-sample\t2026-01-02T00:00:00Z\nrecords/p-2026-01-04-eeeeeee.md\tnone\t2026-01-04T00:00:00Z\n' >"$B/c-index.tsv"
    pick_ctl() { local B=$B/c; mkdir -p "$B" && cp "${B%/c}/c-index.tsv" "$B/rec-index.tsv" && [ "$(pick_record --x-sample)" = records/z-x-2026-01-02-ddddddd.md ] && [ "$(pick_record none)" = records/p-2026-01-04-eeeeeee.md ]; }
    check "control: pick_record takes the latest record time, not the last name, refuses tool arguments that are not exactly the flag, leaves a -scale-<tier>- name out, and reads none for the passthrough (TE)" "$(yn pick_ctl)"
    echo "  the step0-titled records at the phase commit with a record time, indexed: $(count_lines "$B/rec-index.tsv")"
    check "the index holds records" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/rec-index.tsv")" -gt 0 ])"
    # prev_of <name>: the earlier record of the run, part 1 P2's (change WC).
    prev_of() { printf 'records/m8p1-%s-%s.md\n' "$1" "$PREV_TAG"; }
    check "control: prev_of names part 1 P2's record for comment and copy (WC)" "$(yn [ "$(prev_of comment) $(prev_of copy)" = "records/m8p1-comment-$PREV_TAG.md records/m8p1-copy-$PREV_TAG.md" ])"
    # Changes WD, WJ and WU: classify <comparison> <name>: each line of
    # compare_ids's output, prefixed by its class against the expected-change
    # table: met or not (a pair of the table: its own then-triple then and its
    # own now-triple now), kept or moved (a pair named unchanged: its
    # then-triple then and now), same, changed, missing and new. The table is
    # read from EXPECTED_TABLE and KEPT_TABLE at the call (change WU: a then and
    # a now per pair, where P3's EXPECT_THEN and EXPECT_NOW held one for all).
    classify() {
      awk -F'\t' -v OFS='\t' -v name="$2" -v ex="$EXPECTED_TABLE" -v kp="$KEPT_TABLE" '
        BEGIN { n = split(ex, a, " "); for (j = 1; j <= n; j++) { split(a[j], q, ":"); et[q[1] ":" q[2]] = q[3]; en[q[1] ":" q[2]] = q[4] }
          n = split(kp, a, " "); for (j = 1; j <= n; j++) { split(a[j], q, ":"); kt[q[1] ":" q[2]] = q[3] } }
        { kind = $1; id = $2; th = $3; nw = $4; cls = kind; k = name ":" id
          if (k in et) cls = (kind == "changed" && th == et[k] && nw == en[k]) ? "met" : "not"
          else if (k in kt) cls = (kind == "same" && th == kt[k]) ? "kept" : "moved"
          print cls, kind, id, th, nw }' "$1"
    }
    cls_count() { awk -F'\t' -v k="$2" '$1 == k { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$1"; }
    # The fixture: a planted table of two pairs with different triples
    # (aaaaaaaaaaa1 error/-/ok to ok/ok/ok; fffffffffff6 ok/fail/ok to
    # ok/ok/ok) and one named unchanged (ggggggggggg7, error/-/ok); the base
    # lines: the first pair met, an unchanged id, a changed one, a missing one
    # and a new one; then the line each control adds.
    printf '%s\n' "changed${TAB}aaaaaaaaaaa1${TAB}error/-/ok${TAB}ok/ok/ok" "same${TAB}bbbbbbbbbbb2${TAB}ok/ok/ok${TAB}ok/ok/ok" \
      "changed${TAB}ccccccccccc3${TAB}ok/ok/ok${TAB}ok/fail/ok" "missing${TAB}ddddddddddd4${TAB}ok/ok/ok${TAB}-" \
      "new${TAB}eeeeeeeeeee5${TAB}-${TAB}ok/ok/ok" >"$B/c-cls-base"
    cls_fixture() {
      local EXPECTED_TABLE="x-rows:aaaaaaaaaaa1:error/-/ok:ok/ok/ok x-rows:fffffffffff6:ok/fail/ok:ok/ok/ok" KEPT_TABLE="x-rows:ggggggggggg7:error/-/ok" name=${2:-x-rows}
      { cat "$B/c-cls-base"; [ -n "$1" ] && printf '%s\n' "$1"; } >"$B/c-cls-in"
      classify "$B/c-cls-in" "$name" >"$B/c-cls-out"
      printf '%s %s %s %s %s %s\n' "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" met)" "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" not)" \
        "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" same)" "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" changed)" "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" missing)" \
        "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" new)"
    }
    cls_met() { [ "$(cls_fixture "changed${TAB}fffffffffff6${TAB}ok/fail/ok${TAB}ok/ok/ok")" = "2 0 1 1 1 1" ]; }
    cls_unchanged() { [ "$(cls_fixture "same${TAB}fffffffffff6${TAB}ok/fail/ok${TAB}ok/fail/ok")" = "1 1 1 1 1 1" ]; }
    cls_other() { [ "$(cls_fixture "changed${TAB}fffffffffff6${TAB}ok/fail/ok${TAB}error/-/ok")" = "1 1 1 1 1 1" ]; }
    cls_crossed() { [ "$(cls_fixture "changed${TAB}fffffffffff6${TAB}error/-/ok${TAB}ok/ok/ok")" = "1 1 1 1 1 1" ]; }
    cls_sample() { [ "$(cls_fixture "" y-columns)" = "0 0 1 2 1 1" ]; }
    check "classify: two pairs of a table with different triples, each changed by its own then and now, are both met; one each of same, changed, missing and new (changes WD and WU)" "$(yn cls_met)"
    check "control: classify refuses a pair of the table unchanged, its then-triple then and now (change WD)" "$(yn cls_unchanged)"
    check "control: classify refuses a pair of the table changed to another triple (change WD)" "$(yn cls_other)"
    check "control: classify refuses a pair changed by another pair's then-triple, error/-/ok to ok/ok/ok, where its own is ok/fail/ok (change WU)" "$(yn cls_crossed)"
    check "control: outside its sample a pair's id is a plain change, not met (change WD)" "$(yn cls_sample)"
    # Change WJ: a pair named unchanged is kept when it is the same, its
    # then-triple then and now, and moved otherwise.
    cls_kept() { [ "$(cls_fixture "same${TAB}ggggggggggg7${TAB}error/-/ok${TAB}error/-/ok")" = "1 0 1 1 1 1" ] && [ "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" kept)" = 1 ]; }
    cls_moved() { [ "$(cls_fixture "changed${TAB}ggggggggggg7${TAB}error/-/ok${TAB}ok/ok/ok")" = "1 0 1 1 1 1" ] && [ "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" moved)" = 1 ]; }
    cls_kept_other() { [ "$(cls_fixture "same${TAB}ggggggggggg7${TAB}ok/ok/ok${TAB}ok/ok/ok")" = "1 0 1 1 1 1" ] && [ "$(cls_count "$B/c-cls-out" moved)" = 1 ]; }
    check "classify: a pair named unchanged, its then-triple then and now, is kept (change WJ)" "$(yn cls_kept)"
    check "control: classify reads a pair named unchanged that changed as moved (change WJ)" "$(yn cls_moved)"
    check "control: classify reads a pair named unchanged that is the same but not at its then-triple as moved (change WU)" "$(yn cls_kept_other)"
    # Change WU: the table's helpers, on the real table.
    help_ok() {
      [ "$(pair_key "remove:495c7b79b183:ok/fail/ok:ok/ok/ok")" = remove:495c7b79b183 ] \
        && [ "$(entry_then "remove:495c7b79b183:ok/fail/ok:ok/ok/ok") $(entry_now "remove:495c7b79b183:ok/fail/ok:ok/ok/ok")" = "ok/fail/ok ok/ok/ok" ] \
        && [ "$(entry_then "copy:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok")" = error/-/ok ] && [ -z "$(entry_now "copy:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok")" ] \
        && [ "$(table_entry copy:15205770ae5c)" = copy:15205770ae5c:error/-/ok ]
    }
    check "control: pair_key, entry_then, entry_now and table_entry read a change's entry and the unchanged entry (change WU)" "$(yn help_ok)"
    check "control: table_entry reads nothing for a pair the table does not hold" "$(yn [ -z "$(table_entry insert-rows:495c7b79b183)" ])"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## the expected-change table (changes WD, WO and WU)"
    n_table=$(set -- $EXPECTED_PAIRS; echo $#)
    n_kept_table=$(set -- $KEPT_PAIRS; echo $#)
    echo "  the pairs specs/0048 \"Harness runs\" names for P1, P2 and P3, <name>:<id>:<then>:<now>, $n_table:"
    for e in $EXPECTED_TABLE; do echo "    $e"; done
    echo "  the pair it names unchanged, <name>:<id>:<then>, $n_kept_table:"
    for e in $KEPT_TABLE; do echo "    $e"; done
    echo "  the remove pair's line: removed=$EXPECT_REMOVED and removed_reason=$EXPECT_REASON (decision 3 A)"
    check "the table holds six changes and one pair named unchanged, seven pairs, each named once (change WU)" "$(yn [ "$n_table $n_kept_table $(printf '%s\n' $EXPECTED_PAIRS $KEPT_PAIRS | LC_ALL=C sort -u | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = "6 1 7" ])"
    # The spec's sentences at the phase commit, its lines folded to single spaces.
    git show "$C:$SPEC" | tr '\n' ' ' | tr -s ' ' >"$B/spec-folded.txt"
    SPEC_P1_TEXT="P1: the four row and column samples over the 39 workbooks, every output opened, compared per id with part 1 P2's four records: delete-rows 90a5b01f9541 and delete-columns 91d2bdffa46a each error 2 - ok to ok 0 ok ok, nothing else changed."
    SPEC_P2_TEXT='P2: the comment, richcomment, commentbox and copy samples over the 39: the first three on 15205770ae5c error 2 - ok to ok 0 ok ok, copy unchanged (decision 2 A), nothing else changed.'
    SPEC_P3_TEXT='P3: the remove sample over the 39: 495c7b79b183 ok 0 fail ok to ok 0 ok ok with the removed count 0 and `removed_reason` `pivot_source` (decision 3 A; under 3 B error 2 - ok), nothing else changed'
    SPEC_P4_TEXT="P4: the passthrough and the 58 samples over the 39, every output opened, compared per id with part 1 P2's 59 records: the seven changes above and nothing else."
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC, folded to single spaces; the count of each of four sentences:"
    n_spec_ok=0
    for k in P1 P2 P3 P4; do
      var=SPEC_${k}_TEXT
      n=$(count_matches -F "${!var}" "$B/spec-folded.txt")
      echo "  $k: ${!var}"
      echo "    found: $n"
      if [ "$n" = 1 ]; then n_spec_ok=$((n_spec_ok + 1)); fi
    done
    check "the spec at the phase commit names each part's changes and nothing else changed, P1 to P3, and P4's rerun of them, each sentence once (change WU)" "$(yn [ "$n_spec_ok" = 4 ])"
    spec_pairs_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -F "${SPEC_P3_TEXT/495c7b79b183/000000000000}" "$B/spec-folded.txt")" = 0 ]; }
    check "control: the same count reads none for a sentence with an id replaced" "$(yn spec_pairs_ctl)"
    pair_triple() { git show "$C:records/m8p1-${1%%:*}-$PREV_TAG.txt" | triples /dev/stdin | awk -F'\t' -v i="${1#*:}" '$1 == i { print $2 "/" $3 "/" $4 }'; }
    n_pairs_then=0
    for e in $EXPECTED_TABLE $KEPT_TABLE; do
      p=$(pair_key "$e")
      got=$(pair_triple "$p")
      echo "    $p in records/m8p1-${p%%:*}-$PREV_TAG.txt: ${got:-none} (the table's: $(entry_then "$e"))"
      if [ "$got" = "$(entry_then "$e")" ]; then n_pairs_then=$((n_pairs_then + 1)); fi
    done
    check "each pair's triple in part 1 P2's record is the table's then-triple (7 pairs; change WU)" "$(yn [ "$n_pairs_then" = 7 ])"
    check "control: pair_triple reads a pair whose id the record lacks as none" "$(yn [ -z "$(pair_triple delete-rows:000000000000)" ])"
    REMOVE_THEN=$(entry_then "$(table_entry remove:495c7b79b183)")
    pair_ok_ctl() { [ "$(pair_triple insert-rows:495c7b79b183)" = "$REMOVE_THEN" ]; }
    check "control: the remove pair's id in another sample's record (insert-rows) is not $REMOVE_THEN" "$(ynnot pair_ok_ctl)"
    n_met=0
    n_kept=0
    : >"$B/expected-table.tsv"
    # Change WO: line_field <stdout file> <key>: the value of key=value on the
    # remove sample's line (the word remove, then tab-separated pairs), empty
    # when the file, the line or the key is not there.
    line_field() { [ -f "$1" ] || return 0; awk -F'\t' -v k="$2" '$1 == "remove" { for (i = 2; i <= NF; i++) { p = index($i, "="); if (p > 0 && substr($i, 1, p - 1) == k) { print substr($i, p + 1); exit } } }' "$1"; }
    printf 'remove\tsheets_before=2\tremoved=0\tparts=0\tremoved_reason=pivot_source\n' >"$B/c-line.txt"
    printf 'other\tremoved=1\tremoved_reason=-\n' >"$B/c-line2.txt"
    check "control: line_field reads removed 0 and removed_reason pivot_source from a planted remove line (change WO)" "$(yn [ "$(line_field "$B/c-line.txt" removed) $(line_field "$B/c-line.txt" removed_reason)" = "0 pivot_source" ])"
    check "control: line_field reads nothing from a line of another word, a key the line lacks, or a file that is not there (change WO)" "$(yn [ -z "$(line_field "$B/c-line2.txt" removed)$(line_field "$B/c-line.txt" no_such_key)$(line_field "$B/no-such-file" removed)" ])"
    n_line_met=0
    n_pivot=0
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## 3 and 4. the passthrough and the samples on the host, one run each, recorded into <work>/records and compared per id (changes TD, TF, WC, WT and WU)"
    n_want_rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$CORPUS/manifest.tsv" | wc -l)
    echo "  the workbooks each run takes: $n_want_rows (every manifest row)"
    { printf 'passthrough\t-\n'; while IFS= read -r f; do printf '%s\t%s\n' "$(name_of "$f")" "$f"; done <"$B/run.flags"; } >"$B/runs.tsv"
    n_runs_all=$(count_lines "$B/runs.tsv")
    n_done=0
    n_rec_done=0
    n_findings=0
    i=0
    # One run's checks read these, set before each is called: f (the flag, or
    # "-" for the passthrough), name, rrc, RT, rt_rows, rt_commit, rt_args.
    rt_ok() { [ "$rt_rows" = 1 ] && [ "$rt_commit" = "$C" ] && [ "$rt_args" = "$want_args" ]; }
    rt_settings() { [ "$(run_field "$RT" timeout_s)" = "$TIMEOUT_S" ] && [ "$(run_field "$RT" lo_timeout_s)" = "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" ]; }
    rec_ran() { [ "$rrc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$B/record-$name.err" ]; }
    rec_header() {
      [ -f "$RECORDS/$STEM.txt" ] && [ "$(count_matches -xF "- Commit: $C" "$RECORDS/$STEM.md")" = 1 ] \
        && [ "$(count_matches -xF '- Targets: host' "$RECORDS/$STEM.md")" = 1 ] \
        && [ "$(count_matches -xF "- Tool arguments: $rec_args" "$RECORDS/$STEM.md")" = 1 ]
    }
    finding() { echo "  FINDING: $1"; n_findings=$((n_findings + 1)); }
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r name f; do
      i=$((i + 1))
      O=$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$name
      STEM=m8p2-$name-$RUN
      ARGS=()
      if [ "$f" = - ]; then want_args=; rec_args=none; label="the passthrough"; else ARGS=(--tool-arg "$f"); want_args=$f; rec_args=$f; label=$f; fi
      echo
      echo "### $i. $label into <runs>/$RUN-$name"
      echo "command: TMPDIR=<work>/tmp-run scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label host --passthrough <work>/bin/emend-copy --xlsx-diff <work>/bin/xlsx-diff --corpus <corpus> --out <runs>/$RUN-$name --timeout $TIMEOUT_S --libreoffice $IMAGE --lo-timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S ${ARGS[*]}"
      started=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
      TMPDIR=$RUNTMP scripts/passthrough-run.sh --label host --passthrough "$PT" --xlsx-diff "$XD" --corpus "$CORPUS" --out "$O" \
        --timeout "$TIMEOUT_S" --libreoffice "$IMAGE" --lo-timeout "$LO_TIMEOUT_S" "${ARGS[@]}" \
        >"$B/run-$name.stdout" 2>"$B/run-$name.stderr" </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "  started $started; ended $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ); exit $rc; stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/run-$name.stderr")"
      sed 's/^/    /' "$B/run-$name.stdout"
      check "$label: the run exits 0" "$(yn [ "$rc" = 0 ])"
      check "$label: its stderr is empty" "$(yn [ ! -s "$B/run-$name.stderr" ])"
      n_left=$(find "$RUNTMP" -mindepth 1 | wc -l)
      echo "  entries left in <work>/tmp-run after the run: $n_left"
      check "$label: the runs' TMPDIR is empty after the run" "$(yn [ "$n_left" = 0 ])"
      SUM=$O/summary.host.tsv
      RT=$O/run.host.tsv
      if [ ! -f "$SUM" ] || [ ! -f "$RT" ]; then
        check "$label: the run directory holds summary.host.tsv and run.host.tsv" "no"
        continue
      fi
      rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$SUM" | wc -l)
      echo "  summary.host.tsv: rows $rows; outcomes: $(outcome_counts "$SUM")"
      check "$label: the summary holds one row per workbook ($n_want_rows)" "$(yn [ "$rows" = "$n_want_rows" ])"
      rt_rows=$(awk 'NR > 1' "$RT" | wc -l)
      rt_commit=$(run_field "$RT" commit)
      rt_args=$(run_field "$RT" tool_args)
      echo "  run.host.tsv: run rows $rt_rows; commit $rt_commit; tool_args ${rt_args:-(empty)}; timeout_s $(run_field "$RT" timeout_s); lo_timeout_s $(run_field "$RT" lo_timeout_s); memory_mib $(run_field "$RT" memory_mib)"
      check "$label: run.host.tsv holds one run row naming the phase commit and the flag alone" "$(yn rt_ok)"
      check "$label: run.host.tsv names the settings given (timeout $TIMEOUT_S, lo timeout $LO_TIMEOUT_S)" "$(yn rt_settings)"
      n_done=$((n_done + 1))
      echo "command: python3 -I -B scripts/passthrough-record.py --run <runs>/$RUN-$name --out <work>/records --stem $STEM --allow-single"
      python3 -I -B scripts/passthrough-record.py --run "$O" --out "$RECORDS" --stem "$STEM" --allow-single >"$B/record-$name.out" 2>"$B/record-$name.err" </dev/null
      rrc=$?
      echo "  exit: $rrc; stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/record-$name.out"
      echo "  stderr bytes: $(wc -c <"$B/record-$name.err")"
      check "$label: the record script exits 0, its stderr empty" "$(yn rec_ran)"
      check "$label: the record pair is there, its .md naming the phase commit on its Commit: line, the host alone and the tool arguments $rec_args" "$(yn rec_header)"
      if [ ! -f "$RECORDS/$STEM.txt" ]; then continue; fi
      echo "  record (written in <work>/records, installed in section 5; change WV): $STEM.md sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS/$STEM.md"); $STEM.txt sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS/$STEM.txt")"
      n_rec_done=$((n_rec_done + 1))
      triples "$RECORDS/$STEM.txt" >"$B/now-$name.tri"
      triples "$SUM" >"$B/sum-$name.tri"
      check "$label: the record's host triples are the summary's" "$(yn cmp -s "$B/now-$name.tri" "$B/sum-$name.tri")"
      # Change WC: the earlier record, part 1 P2's.
      prev=$(prev_of "$name")
      picked=$(pick_record "$rec_args")
      echo "  the earlier record: $prev (change WC); the one the selection rule picks at the phase commit: ${picked:-none}"
      if [ "$picked" != "$prev" ]; then
        finding "$label: the selection rule picks ${picked:-no record}, not part 1 P2's $prev; part 1 P2's is compared (WC)"
      fi
      if git cat-file -e "$C:${prev%.md}.txt" 2>/dev/null; then :; else
        finding "$label: the earlier record ${prev%.md}.txt is not at the phase commit; nothing is compared"
        continue
      fi
      git show "$C:${prev%.md}.txt" >"$B/prev/$name.txt" || exit 2
      triples "$B/prev/$name.txt" >"$B/prev-$name.tri"
      compare_ids "$B/prev-$name.tri" "$B/now-$name.tri" "$B/cmp-$name.tsv"
      classify "$B/cmp-$name.tsv" "$name" >"$B/cls-$name.tsv"
      n_then=$(count_lines "$B/prev-$name.tri")
      n_same=$(kind_count "$B/cmp-$name.tsv" same)
      n_changed=$(kind_count "$B/cmp-$name.tsv" changed)
      n_missing=$(kind_count "$B/cmp-$name.tsv" missing)
      n_new=$(kind_count "$B/cmp-$name.tsv" new)
      echo "  compared with ${prev%.md}.txt per id (outcome/lo/lo_in of the host rows): earlier ids $n_then; the same $n_same; changed $n_changed; missing from this run $n_missing; new ids $n_new"
      n_met_here=0
      while IFS="$TAB" read -r cls kind id then_t now_t; do
        case $cls in
          met)
            n_met_here=$((n_met_here + 1))
            n_met=$((n_met + 1))
            echo "    expected (specs/0048 \"Harness runs\"): $name:$id: $then_t then, $now_t now" ;;
          not) te=$(table_entry "$name:$id"); finding "$label: id $id: outcome/lo/lo_in $then_t in ${prev##*/}, $now_t now, not the change specs/0048 names ($(entry_then "$te") to $(entry_now "$te")); recorded, not fixed" ;;
          kept)
            n_kept=$((n_kept + 1))
            echo "    expected unchanged (specs/0048 \"Harness runs\" P2, decision 2 A): $name:$id: $then_t then and now" ;;
          moved) te=$(table_entry "$name:$id"); finding "$label: id $id: outcome/lo/lo_in $then_t in ${prev##*/}, $now_t now, where specs/0048 names it unchanged ($(entry_then "$te")); recorded, not fixed" ;;
          changed) finding "$label: id $id: outcome/lo/lo_in $then_t in ${prev##*/}, $now_t now; recorded, not fixed" ;;
          missing)
            if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then finding "$label: id $id of ${prev##*/} ($then_t) is not in this run"
            else echo "    a dry run: id $id of ${prev##*/} is not in the fictional corpus; not judged"; fi ;;
          new)
            if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then finding "$label: id $id ($now_t) is not in ${prev##*/}"
            else echo "    a dry run: id $id ($now_t) is not in ${prev##*/}; printed"; fi ;;
        esac
      done <"$B/cls-$name.tsv"
      # A pair of the table whose id is not in this run's comparison at all.
      for p in $EXPECTED_PAIRS $KEPT_PAIRS; do
        if [ "${p%%:*}" = "$name" ] && [ "$(awk -F'\t' -v i="${p#*:}" '$3 == i' "$B/cls-$name.tsv" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; then
          if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then finding "$label: the table's id ${p#*:} is in neither record"
          else echo "    a dry run: the table's id ${p#*:} is not in the fictional corpus; not judged"; fi
        fi
      done
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$label" "$n_met_here" >>"$B/expected-table.tsv"
      # Change WO: the sample's line for every id, read from the run directory's
      # <id>/stdout.host.txt: the reasons counted; each pair of the table must
      # read removed 0 and pivot_source; a pivot_source on an id outside the
      # table is a FINDING in the logged run and printed in a dry run.
      if [ "$name" = remove ]; then
        : >"$B/reasons-$name.tsv"
        while IFS= read -r id; do
          printf '%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$(line_field "$O/$id/stdout.host.txt" removed)" "$(line_field "$O/$id/stdout.host.txt" removed_reason)" >>"$B/reasons-$name.tsv"
        done < <(awk -F'\t' 'NR == 1 { for (i = 1; i <= NF; i++) if ($i == "id") k = i; next } k { print $k }' "$SUM")
        echo "  the sample's line per id, by removed_reason (the empty reason for an id with no remove line): $(awk -F'\t' '{ n[($3 == "" ? "(none)" : $3)]++ } END { for (k in n) print k, n[k] }' "$B/reasons-$name.tsv" | LC_ALL=C sort | tr '\n' ' ')"
        while IFS="$TAB" read -r id removed reason; do
          in_table=no
          case " $EXPECTED_PAIRS " in *" $name:$id "*) in_table=yes ;; esac
          if [ "$in_table" = yes ]; then
            if [ "$removed/$reason" = "$EXPECT_REMOVED/$EXPECT_REASON" ]; then
              n_line_met=$((n_line_met + 1))
              echo "    expected (specs/0048 \"Harness runs\" P3, decision 3 A): id $id: removed=$removed removed_reason=$reason"
            else
              finding "$label: id $id: removed=${removed:-none} removed_reason=${reason:-none}, not removed=$EXPECT_REMOVED removed_reason=$EXPECT_REASON (decision 3 A); recorded, not fixed"
            fi
          elif [ "$reason" = "$EXPECT_REASON" ]; then
            n_pivot=$((n_pivot + 1))
            if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then finding "$label: id $id reads removed_reason=$reason and is not in the table; recorded, not fixed"
            else echo "    a dry run: id $id reads removed_reason=$reason, a fixture outside the table; printed, not judged"; fi
          fi
        done <"$B/reasons-$name.tsv"
        for p in $EXPECTED_PAIRS; do
          if [ "${p%%:*}" = "$name" ] && [ "$(awk -F'\t' -v i="${p#*:}" '$1 == i' "$B/reasons-$name.tsv" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; then
            if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then finding "$label: the table's id ${p#*:} has no row in this run's summary"
            else echo "    a dry run: the table's id ${p#*:} is not in the fictional corpus; its line is not judged"; fi
          fi
        done
      fi
      if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then
        check "$label: the earlier record holds 39 host rows, this run 39, and no id is new or missing (WQ)" "$(yn [ "$n_then $rows $n_new $n_missing" = "39 39 0 0" ])"
      fi
      echo "  summary $label: earlier $n_then (same $n_same, changed $n_changed, missing $n_missing); new $n_new; the table's pairs met here $n_met_here; their lines met $n_line_met; other ids reading pivot_source $n_pivot; FINDING lines so far $n_findings"
    done <"$B/runs.tsv"
    echo
    echo "  runs done $n_done of $n_runs_all (the passthrough and $n_run flags); record pairs written $n_rec_done; FINDING lines so far: $n_findings"
    check "every run was made, and its run directory holds its tables" "$(yn [ "$n_done" = "$n_runs_all" ])"
    check "every run was recorded" "$(yn [ "$n_rec_done" = "$n_runs_all" ])"
    echo "  the run directories, the passthrough's first and the flags' in the usage text's order:"
    n_dirs_there=0
    while IFS="$TAB" read -r name f; do
      if [ -d "$RUN_OUT_ROOT/$RUN-$name" ]; then n_dirs_there=$((n_dirs_there + 1)); st=there; else st=MISSING; fi
      printf '    <runs>/%s-%s %s\n' "$RUN" "$name" "$st"
    done <"$B/runs.tsv"
    echo "  run directories there: $n_dirs_there"
    check "one run directory per run is there" "$(yn [ "$n_dirs_there" = "$n_runs_all" ])"
    
    # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    echo
    echo "## 5. the record pairs installed into $RECORDS_DEST/ (change WV: part 1 P2's section 5)"
    ls "$RECORDS" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$B/records.names"
    n_rec=$(count_lines "$B/records.names")
    want_rec=$((2 * n_runs_all))
    echo "  record files written in <work>/records: $n_rec; expected $want_rec (a pair per run)"
    check "the record files are the pairs expected" "$(yn [ "$n_rec" = "$want_rec" ])"
    check "the record files are two per run directory" "$(yn [ "$n_rec" = "$((2 * n_dirs_there))" ])"
    if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then
      check "the record files are 118 and the run directories 59 (the passthrough and 58 flags: 59 less --new-sample; change WX)" "$(yn [ "$n_rec $n_dirs_there" = "118 59" ])"
    fi
    rec_names_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -E "^m8p2-[a-z0-9-]+-$RUN[.](md|txt)\$" "$B/records.names")" = "$n_rec" ]; }
    check "every record file is named m8p2-<name>-$RUN.md or .txt (change WV)" "$(yn rec_names_ok)"
    printf 'm8p2-remove-%s.md\nm8p1-remove-%s.md\nm8p2-remove-%s.txt.bak\n' "$RUN" "$RUN" "$RUN" >"$B/c-rec-names"
    rec_names_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E "^m8p2-[a-z0-9-]+-$RUN[.](md|txt)\$" "$B/c-rec-names")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form takes a planted m8p2 name and refuses another phase's and a third suffix" "$(yn rec_names_ctl)"
    no_path() { [ "$(cat "$RECORDS/"* | count_matches -F "$HOME" /dev/stdin)" = 0 ] && [ "$(cat "$RECORDS/"* | count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "no record file names <home>, a home, mount, temporary or corpus path" "$(yn no_path)"
    printf '%s%s%s\n' '/ho' 'me/someone/' 'emend-testing/corpus/x' >"$B/c-path"
    path_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E '(/home/|/mnt/|/Users/|/tmp/|emend-testing)' "$B/c-path")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form finds a planted path" "$(yn path_ctl)"
    mkdir -p "$RECORDS_DEST" || exit 2
    n_inst=0
    while IFS= read -r f; do
      if [ -e "$RECORDS_DEST/$f" ]; then echo "    $RECORDS_DEST/$f is already there: not installed"; continue; fi
      install -m 644 "$RECORDS/$f" "$RECORDS_DEST/$f" || continue
      cmp -s "$RECORDS/$f" "$RECORDS_DEST/$f" && n_inst=$((n_inst + 1))
      echo "    installed $RECORDS_DEST/$f: sha256 $(sha_of "$RECORDS_DEST/$f"), $(wc -c <"$RECORDS_DEST/$f") bytes"
    done <"$B/records.names"
    check "every record file was installed, byte for byte" "$(yn [ "$n_inst" = "$n_rec" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the expected-change table (specs/0048 \"Harness runs\" P1 to P4; changes WU and WX)"
    echo "  per run: the run, the table's pairs met in it:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/expected-table.tsv"
    echo "  the table's pairs met: $n_met of $n_table; the remove pair's line met (removed $EXPECT_REMOVED, removed_reason $EXPECT_REASON): $n_line_met of 1; other ids reading $EXPECT_REASON: $n_pivot; the pair named unchanged and kept: $n_kept of $n_kept_table"
    if [ "$LOGGED" = yes ]; then
      check "the six pairs of the table are met, each by its own then and now, the remove pair's line reads removed $EXPECT_REMOVED and removed_reason $EXPECT_REASON, no other id reads $EXPECT_REASON, and copy 15205770ae5c is kept error/-/ok (WX)" "$(yn [ "$n_met.$n_line_met.$n_pivot.$n_kept" = 6.1.0.1 ])"
    else
      echo "  a dry run: the totals are printed and not judged (WX)"
    fi
    met_ctl() { local n_met=6 n_line_met=0 n_pivot=0 n_kept=1; [ "$n_met.$n_line_met.$n_pivot.$n_kept" = 6.1.0.1 ]; }
    check "control: the same total refuses the pairs met without the remove pair's line" "$(ynnot met_ctl)"
    met_ctl2() { local n_met=6 n_line_met=1 n_pivot=1 n_kept=1; [ "$n_met.$n_line_met.$n_pivot.$n_kept" = 6.1.0.1 ]; }
    check "control: the same total refuses another id reading $EXPECT_REASON" "$(ynnot met_ctl2)"
    met_ctl3() { local n_met=6 n_line_met=1 n_pivot=0 n_kept=0; [ "$n_met.$n_line_met.$n_pivot.$n_kept" = 6.1.0.1 ]; }
    check "control: the same total refuses the copy pair not kept" "$(ynnot met_ctl3)"
    met_ctl4() { local n_met=5 n_line_met=1 n_pivot=0 n_kept=1; [ "$n_met.$n_line_met.$n_pivot.$n_kept" = 6.1.0.1 ]; }
    check "control: the same total refuses five pairs met of six" "$(ynnot met_ctl4)"
    
    echo
    echo "## the FINDING lines of this log (specs/0043 ruling R)"
    echo "  FINDING lines printed above: $n_findings (each begins with the word FINDING; the comparisons print them, none is fixed)"
    
    echo
    echo "## status after the run"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    echo "  the working spec: $SPEC, sha256 $(sha_of "$SPEC")"
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them this phase's logs, its record files or planning's spec and ROADMAP.md: $st_ours"
    status_accounted() { [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" != error ] && [ "$st_all" = "$st_ours" ]; }
    check "every change in the working tree is this phase's or planning's" "$(yn status_accounted)"
    st_rec=$(run_matches -E '^[?][?] records/m8p2-' git status --porcelain)
    echo "  this phase's record files untracked in the repository's records/: $st_rec"
    # Change WV: a logged run's installed files are untracked in records/, one
    # status line each; a dry run's went to RUN_RECORDS_DEST, so none is there.
    if [ "$RECORDS_DEST" = records ]; then
      check "the record files installed are untracked in records/, one status line each ($n_inst; change WV)" "$(yn [ "$st_rec" = "$n_inst" ])"
    else
      check "a dry run's records went to RUN_RECORDS_DEST: none of this phase's is in the repository's records/ (change WV)" "$(yn [ "$st_rec" = 0 ])"
    fi
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    cp "$ERR" "$B/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$B/c-err"
    nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$B/c-err")
    echo "  command: wc -c <scripts>/out/run.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "run log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources (the phase commit's, by git show)
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

